{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-1: If Google authentication succeeds but the employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved from the corporate directory, deny access and return a retryable error with a contact path.","ASM-2 and ASM-13: A returning employee without a saved plate resumes vehicle registration and cannot proceed to the dashboard until at least one plate is saved.","ASM-3: The corporate directory is authoritative for employee identity; parking administrators maintain assignments, floors, and vehicle details in the app.","ASM-4: Unreadable or unverifiable plates do not authorize entry, do not activate the green indicator, and are recorded with the failure reason.","ASM-5, ASM-17, and ASM-18: Camera, authorization, or indicator unavailability fails closed; no temporary entry authorization is issued and the outage or failed attempt is recorded.","ASM-6 and ASM-19: Administrators use admin-only screens in the same app; guard and administrator interfaces are responsive web interfaces for desktop and mobile browsers.","ASM-7: 'Today,' the 30-day scheduling window, and the Daily Parking Release Time use the office location's local timezone and calendar day.","ASM-10 and ASM-22: Initial user-facing content is English and left-to-right.","ASM-11 and ASM-23: The accessibility target is WCAG 2.1 AA on main flows.","ASM-14: Administrator plate changes affect future dates; existing claims retain the plate recorded when the claim was created.","ASM-15: An employee without dedicated parking may have at most one temporary claim per date.","ASM-16: An administrator may revoke a claimed release and restore the dedicated holder's use for the remainder of that date.","ASM-24: For the weekly report, the report period is the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday week in the office-local timezone.","ASM-25: Overall utilization percentage is calculated as unique parking-space days with a recorded actual entry divided by total active parking-space days in the report period, multiplied by 100."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"100% of audited main-flow screens pass applicable WCAG 2.1 Level AA success criteria.","text":"Main employee, guard, and administrator flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA."}],"outOfScope":["Custom report builder (ASM-8, ASM-9)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has an authorized Folio3 Google Workspace account and an assigned application role","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned record contains the assigned role","when":"the user completes Google sign-in"},{"given":"A user signs in with a personal Gmail account or another non-Folio3 account","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 401 and no application session record is returned","when":"the authentication callback is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall accept sign-in only through authorized Folio3 Google Workspace accounts for employees, security guards, and parking administrators, rejecting personal Gmail and other provider accounts.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","Q-7"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has a corporate-directory record and parking data entered in the app","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"api","then":"the returned record contains the directory employee ID and name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle list","when":"the employee profile is retrieved"},{"given":"A parking administrator changes an employee's registered plate after a temporary claim has been created","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"api","then":"the claim record contains the plate captured for that claim and the employee profile row contains the updated plate for future dates","when":"the claim record is retrieved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall identify employees by corporate email, retrieve employee ID and name from the corporate directory, and associate those identity fields with app-maintained dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and one or more registered vehicle profiles.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-3"],"stability":0.86},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated non-dedicated employee has no saved plate","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 409 and the returned registration state requires at least one plate","when":"the employee requests the dashboard"},{"given":"An employee submits a vehicle profile with a plate and omits make, model, and color","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the vehicle row contains the plate with empty optional fields","when":"the profile is saved"}],"ears":"If a non-dedicated employee has no registered vehicle plate, then the Folio3 Parking System shall require at least one plate to be saved before making the dashboard available, while allowing vehicle make, model, and color to be optional and directing an incomplete returning profile to registration.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-13"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Google authentication succeeded but the employee profile is missing or unavailable","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403, the error value is retryable, a contact path is returned, and no application session record exists","when":"the system completes profile lookup"}],"ears":"If Google authentication succeeds but the employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved from the corporate directory, then the Folio3 Parking System shall deny application access and return a retryable error with a contact path.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee, security guard, or parking administrator is authenticated","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"api","then":"the response list contains only the employee's own records for an employee, verification information for a guard, and permitted managed records for an administrator","when":"each role requests employee and parking records"},{"given":"A security guard requests an administration function or an employee requests another employee's record","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403 and no restricted record is returned","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall restrict employees to their own records, limit guards to information needed for entry verification, and permit administrators to manage records and access configured reports.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-5","Q-1"],"stability":0.82},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator submits an initial employee parking assignment, floor, and vehicle","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the corresponding parking-assignment and vehicle rows contain the submitted values","when":"the administrator saves the records"},{"given":"A non-administrator submits an assignment or vehicle maintenance request","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403 and no record is changed","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow parking administrators to enter and maintain parking assignments, assigned floors, and registered vehicles, including initial launch records, with plate changes applying to future dates while existing claims retain their recorded plate.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","Q-5","ASM-3","ASM-6","ASM-14"],"stability":0.86},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A person checks the employee application on supported mobile platforms","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"manual","then":"the employee sign-in screen is displayed on each platform","when":"the application is installed and opened on iOS and Android devices"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall provide employee mobile applications for both iOS and Android.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A guard or administrator signs in using a desktop browser and a mobile browser","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"manual","then":"the verification or administrator screen is displayed and its controls remain available at both viewport sizes","when":"the user opens the role-specific application"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall provide security guards and parking administrators responsive web interfaces for desktop and mobile browsers, with administration functions available on administrator-only screens in the same app.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-5","ASM-6","ASM-19"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens an employee, guard, or administrator screen","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"manual","then":"the visible user-facing content is in English and laid out left-to-right","when":"the screen is displayed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall display user-facing application content in English using left-to-right text.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-10","ASM-22"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder has not released today's parking","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned parking status is Released","when":"the holder submits the release action"},{"given":"A dedicated holder opens the employee home screen","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows a single release action and displays the resulting parking status","when":"the holder releases today's parking"},{"given":"A non-holder or a holder who has already released today's parking submits a release request","id":"AC-REQ-10.3","level":"api","then":"the response indicates an error and the parking row count for that holder and date remains one","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall let only a dedicated parking holder release today's parking through a single home-screen release action, prevent duplicate releases for the same holder and date, and expose the current Reserved, Released, or Claimed status.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder selects a date 30 local calendar days ahead","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and a release row exists for the selected date","when":"the holder saves the scheduled release"},{"given":"A dedicated holder selects a date 31 local calendar days ahead","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 422 and no release row exists for that date","when":"the holder submits the scheduled release"},{"given":"A dedicated holder opens the release calendar","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows the selected dates as scheduled releases","when":"the holder selects and saves multiple dates within the 30-day window"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall let dedicated holders schedule releases for one or multiple future dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and persist each selected release.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-7"],"stability":0.87},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No administrator has changed the Daily Parking Release Time","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"api","then":"the returned value is 08:00 in the office-local timezone","when":"the configuration is retrieved"},{"given":"A release is scheduled for today or is submitted before the configured time","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"api","then":"the release row status is Claimable","when":"the configured Daily Parking Release Time is reached"},{"given":"A holder submits a same-day release at or after the configured time","id":"AC-REQ-12.3","level":"api","then":"the release row status is Claimable and the available-space count is updated","when":"the release is saved"},{"given":"An administrator submits a new Daily Parking Release Time","id":"AC-REQ-12.4","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned configuration contains the new time","when":"the configuration is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall use a configurable Daily Parking Release Time defaulting to 08:00 office-local time, make pre-scheduled releases and same-day releases created before that time claimable at that time, and make same-day releases created at or after that time claimable immediately.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-7"],"stability":0.86},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A scheduled release has not been claimed","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the release row status is Cancelled","when":"the holder cancels it"},{"given":"A scheduled release has been claimed","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains an error and the claim row remains active","when":"the holder attempts cancellation"},{"given":"An administrator revokes a temporary claim after the dedicated release was claimed","id":"AC-REQ-13.3","level":"api","then":"the claim row is Revoked and the dedicated holder's parking row is Restored for the remainder of that date","when":"the revocation is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow a holder to cancel an unclaimed scheduled release, deny holder cancellation after a claim, and allow an administrator to revoke that claim and restore the holder's use for the remainder of the date.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-16"],"stability":0.84},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One or more spaces become claimable and eligible employees without dedicated parking exist","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains the refreshed available-space count and an outbound call to the push notification service is sent to eligible employees","when":"availability is updated"},{"given":"An employee opens the availability view","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the current available-space count","when":"the view is loaded"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall publish the current available-space count and send a push notification to eligible employees without dedicated parking whenever one or more spaces become claimable.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"],"stability":0.83},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Two eligible employees concurrently request the last available space","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"api","then":"the first accepted request has a successful response, the later response contains an error, and the later response includes the refreshed available-space count","when":"the service accepts the requests in a defined order"},{"given":"An employee already has a temporary claim for a date or has dedicated parking","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains an error and the claim row count for that employee and date remains one","when":"the employee requests another temporary claim for that date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee request accepted by the service, limit each employee to one temporary claim per date, and return refreshed availability to later unsuccessful claimants.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-3","ASM-15"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An eligible employee successfully claims an available space","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains the assigned floor and a claim row contains the date, time, employee, and assigned-space fields","when":"the claim is completed"},{"given":"A claim is returned to an employee","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the assigned floor without requiring floor-arrival confirmation","when":"the employee views the claim"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall assign one available parking space and its floor to a successful claimant, record the claim date, time, employee, and assigned space for audit, and not require proof that the employee parked on the assigned floor.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"],"stability":0.84},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has an active temporary claim","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200, the claim row status is Cancelled, and the available-space count increases immediately","when":"the employee cancels the claim"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow an employee to cancel a successful temporary claim at any time and make the claimed space available immediately.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-6"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The LPR camera sends car, pedestrian, motorcycle, and other non-car detections","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"api","then":"the returned event list contains car detections and contains no verification request for the non-car detections","when":"the detection events are processed"},{"given":"A vehicle is marked as having a permanent parking sticker","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"api","then":"the verification request count is zero and no temporary authorization call is made","when":"its entrance event is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall process license-plate-recognition detections for cars, ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects, and bypass temporary system verification for vehicles marked with a permanent parking sticker.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A temporary claim is active for today and the detected plate is any plate registered to its claimant for the claimed date","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"api","then":"the authorization response is valid and an outbound call to the indicator controller requests green","when":"the plate is verified"},{"given":"A detected plate has no valid temporary claim for today","id":"AC-REQ-19.2","level":"api","then":"the authorization response is invalid and the green-indicator activation call count is zero","when":"the plate is verified"}],"ears":"Where a readable plate is detected on an unstickered vehicle, the Folio3 Parking System shall