ry record","id":"AC-REQ-22.1","level":"job","then":"a utilization event row identifies the employee, vehicle, date, and Unused Dedicated Parking or Unused Temporary Parking classification as applicable","when":"the utilization job processes the date"},{"given":"A camera detection or authorization exists without a guard-recorded actual entry","id":"AC-REQ-22.2","level":"job","then":"the utilization event row does not classify the parking as utilized solely from that detection or authorization","when":"the utilization job processes the date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall use recorded actual-entry outcomes, rather than camera detections or authorization attempts alone, to preserve utilization history and identify dedicated parking that was not released and had no entry and temporary claims that had no entry.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-4"],"stability":0.85},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The weekly reporting job is due on Monday morning and recipient addresses are configured","id":"AC-REQ-23.1","level":"job","then":"the report record covers the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday office-local week and contains the required employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space count, temporary-claim count, and numeric utilization percentage","when":"the reporting job runs"},{"given":"The weekly reporting job runs on Monday morning","id":"AC-REQ-23.2","level":"job","then":"an outbound call to the email delivery service contains the report and is addressed to every configured stakeholder","when":"the report is generated"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall generate and email a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office-local timezone to configured stakeholders, containing unused dedicated and temporary parking employees, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and temporary-claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-24","ASM-25"],"stability":0.76},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated administrator submits stakeholder email addresses","id":"AC-REQ-24.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the recipient-list row contains the submitted addresses","when":"the recipient list is saved"},{"given":"An administrator opens report settings in the app","id":"AC-REQ-24.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the saved recipient list","when":"the administrator updates the stakeholder list"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow parking administrators to add, update, and remove the stakeholder list used for weekly utilization report emails in the app.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-8","ASM-6"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The utilization job processes unused dedicated or temporary parking events","id":"AC-REQ-25.1","level":"job","then":"the utilization event rows exist and the warning, suspension, and penalty outbound call counts are zero","when":"the job completes"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization events.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"],"stability":0.92}],"suggestions":["Confirm the definition of an active parking-space day and the utilization percentage formula with parking stakeholders before acceptance testing; the stated formula is an explicit assumption."]}],"models":["gpt-6-luna"],"notes":[]}